## Why This Is Asked

This question tests the ability to translate policy into a concrete routing mechanism with auditability for multi-tenant enterprise chat systems.

## Key Concepts

- Signals: data-sensitivity, intent, policy-violations
- Modes: taboo-free, context-constrained, escalate
- Validation: unit tests with synthetic prompts and edge cases

## Code Example

```javascript
// Minimal prototype
function analyze(p){
  return { policyViolation: false, redacted: false };
}
function routePrompt(p){
  const s = analyze(p);
  if (s.policyViolation) return { mode: 'escalate', reason: 'policy' };
  if (s.redacted) return { mode: 'context-constrained', reason: 'redaction' };
  return { mode: 'taboo-free' };
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you log decisions for audits without leaking PII?
- How would you detect drift in routing quality over time?

## Why This Is Asked

Tests ability to design a modular, auditable routing layer for prompts with data-sensitivity and reproducibility concerns. It emphasizes concrete signals, edge-case handling, and a small prototype to demonstrate flow control.

## Key Concepts

- Prompt routing signals: intent, data_sensitivity, reproducibility
- Edge-case handling: ambiguity, missing sources, conflicting data
- Lightweight prototyping: minimal module map and payload schema

## Code Example

```javascript
function routePrompt(prompt) {
  const text = prompt.toLowerCase()
  const toLiterature = /(summarize|literature|research)/.test(text)
  const toExperiment = /(experiment|plan|propose)/.test(text)
  const needsAudit = /(audit|trace|reproducible)/.test(text)

  if (toLiterature && toExperiment && needsAudit) {
    return {
      modules: ['Literature-Summary', 'Experiment-Plan', 'Audit-Log-Formatter'],
      payload: { prompt, sources: [], trace: { confidence: 0.8 } }
    }
  }
  // Additional routing logic...
}
```

## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design multi-tenant prompt systems, policy-driven routing, and drift auditing; checks comfort with latency budgeting and audit trails; reveals understanding of safety constraints.

## Key Concepts
- Multi-tenant policy blobs
- Model routing via data_classifications
- Safety guard injection preserving intent
- Drift detection and latency budgeting
- Audit log design and replayability

## Code Example
```javascript
// Minimal prototype illustrating routing and rewriting
function routePrompt(prompt, tenantPolicy, models) {
  // decide avatar
  const avatar = tenantPolicy.data_classifications.includes('medical') ? models.avatarA : models.avatarB;
  // rewrite to inject guard
  const guarded = `Guarded: ${prompt} [guard:${tenantPolicy.allowed_actions.join(',')}]`;
  // fake latency
  return { guarded, avatar: avatar.name };
}
```

